Article 49
(1) Special protection for children in conflict with the law as referred to in Article 44 includes children in conflict with the law and child victims of criminal acts, and constitutes the obligation and responsibility of the Regional Government and society.
- 30 - (2) Special protection for children in conflict with the law as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented through:
a. treatment of children in a humane manner in accordance with the dignity and rights of children;
b. provision of special accompanying officers for children from an early stage; c. provision of special facilities and infrastructure;
d. imposition of appropriate sanctions for the best interests of the child;
e. continuous monitoring and recording of the development of children in conflict with the law; f. provision of guarantees to maintain relationships with parents or family; and
g. protection from disclosure of identity through mass media and to avoid labeling.
(3) Special protection for children who become victims of criminal acts as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented through:
a. rehabilitation efforts, both within institutions and outside institutions;
b. efforts to protect from disclosure of identity through mass media and to avoid labeling;
c. provision of safety guarantees for victim witnesses and expert witnesses, whether physical, mental, or social; and
d. provision of accessibility to obtain information regarding case developments.

